---
import StandardLifecycleNotice from "../../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import StandardPageLayout from "../../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../../data/standards/hgb/drs12.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  subtitle={metadata.nativeTitle}
  framework="hgb"
  status={metadata.status}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Part of the DRS consolidation wave" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Why withdrawn" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Status summary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <StandardLifecycleNotice
    type="withdrawn"
    explanation="This standard has been withdrawn."
    targetStatus="Replaced by DRS 24"
    link="/germany/drs/drs24"
    linkText="View DRS 24"
  />

  <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Part of the DRS consolidation wave</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card warn">
<div class="ctitle">Part of the DRS consolidation wave</div>
<div class="principle">DRS 12 addressed the recognition and measurement of intangible assets within the fixed-asset category, supplementing the general HGB framework (§§246, 248, 255, established in the earlier HGB poster series) — a genuinely important area given the recurring interpretive challenges around self-created intangibles, brand values, and similar items arising in practice.</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Why withdrawn — folded into the 2016 group-accounts-specific rewrite</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card info">
<div class="ctitle">Why withdrawn — folded into the 2016 group-accounts-specific rewrite</div>
<div class="principle">DRS 12 was withdrawn effective for fiscal years beginning after 31 December 2016, replaced by DRS 24 "Immaterielle Vermögensgegenstände im Konzernabschluss" — part of the SAME coordinated 23 February 2016 release that also introduced DRS 22 and DRS 23. DRS 24's own explicit focus on the CONSOLIDATION-specific dimension (particularly purchase-price allocation following a business acquisition) reflects a genuine shift in emphasis toward group-accounting particulars, rather than simply restating DRS 12's own more general treatment.</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Status summary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card">
<div class="ctitle">Status summary</div>
<div class="td-table">
<div class="th"><span>Field</span><span>Detail</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Original topic</span><span>Intangible fixed assets, general treatment</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Withdrawn</span><span>Effective for fiscal years beginning after 31.12.2016</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Successor</span><span><strong>DRS 24 — Immaterielle Vermögensgegenstände im Konzernabschluss</strong> (group-accounts focus, particularly purchase-price allocation)</span></div>
</div>
</div>
  </div>

</StandardPageLayout>
